# Line endings.
#
# Both clones of this project were made on Windows without core.autocrlf set,
# so every text file arrived with CRLF while the repository stores LF. Git read
# that as a full rewrite of every file — 109 files and 24,784 lines in one repo,
# 27 in the other, with zero real change. A commit made from that state would
# have buried the actual edit and destroyed git blame.
#
# Local config fixes it for one clone on one machine. This file fixes it for
# every clone, every machine, and the CI runner, because it travels with the
# repository.
#
# text=auto: normalise to LF inside the repository, check out native line
# endings in the working tree (CRLF on Windows). Nothing on disk changes for
# anyone working today.
* text=auto

# Binaries: never transform. Git's auto-detection already catches these, but
# card images and fonts are the files that would be silently corrupted if it
# ever guessed wrong, so state it.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.mp4  binary
